  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive). No transitive pair.\n\nASPECT: ている indicates a completed departure (resultative). {旅立|たびだ}っている = 'has departed.'\n\nUSAGE:\nMore literary and emotional than {出発|しゅっぱつ}する (to depart). Often implies a significant or life-changing journey, not just going on vacation. The euphemistic sense (sense 2) is commonly used in obituaries and condolence contexts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {故郷|ふるさと}から{旅立|たびだ}つ: to leave one's hometown\n- {新天地|しんてんち}へ{旅立|たびだ}つ: to set out for a new land\n- {静|しず}かに{旅立|たびだ}つ: to pass away quietly\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {出発|しゅっぱつ}する: to depart (neutral, practical)\n- {発|た}つ: to depart, to leave (general)\n- {旅立|たびだ}ち: departure on a journey (noun form)",
